  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Suppose \\(A > B > 0\\) and \\(A\\) is \\(x\\%\\) greater than \\(B.\\) What is \\(x?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\( 100\\left(\\frac{A-B}{B}\\right) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\( 100\\left(\\frac{A+B}{B}\\right) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\( 100\\left(\\frac{A+B}{A}\\right) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\( 100\\left(\\frac{A-B}{A}\\right) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\( 100\\left(\\frac{A}{B}\\right) \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2014-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By definition, we know \\[A = \\dfrac {x+ 100}{100}B \\]\\[= B + \\dfrac x{100}B.\\]\n\nThis implies, \\[\\begin{aligned} (A-B) &= \\dfrac x{100}B\\\\ 100\\left(\\dfrac{A-B} B\\right) &=x.\\end{aligned}\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is A .",
      "hints": [
        "Percent greater is measured relative to the smaller value \\(B\\)",
        "First find the fraction \\(\\frac{A-B}{B}\\)"
      ],
